                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This was one of those games you remember from childhood very fondly. I only rediscovered this game around the summer of 2025 after about 20 years of wondering what game it was. After finally playing it again, I can definitely say that this is one of those games you remember positively as a kid because you don't really have an understanding of 'quality'. \n\nWhile I like the UI and visuals having that early to mid 2000s PC game charm, the game itself plays extremely slowly with building the first hut probably being one of the worst parts of the game. Actual progression is also terribly slow with minigames meant to hold you out. the variety of minigames is definitely nice but it doesn't save it the game itself. Trying to finish the game is also extremely cryptic requiring me to scour the internet for a guide on all the radio parts only for an ending that either has you continuing your current playthrough or just immediately thrown into a new one without fanfare or a conclusion for the previous one. \n\nAll in all, definitely better as a distant memory rather something worth replaying.",
